          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 31-year-old male patient, admitted on 21/11/2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection. On admission, he presented with fever, dry cough, and progressive dyspnoea. Chest X-ray and CT thorax revealed bilateral ground-glass opacities consistent with COVID-19 pneumonia. Blood tests and arterial blood gases confirmed hypoxaemia. Pulse oximetry monitoring was performed continuously. The patient received supplemental oxygen therapy, antiviral and anti-inflammatory medication (dexamethasone), and intravenous fluids. Respiratory physiotherapy was initiated. He improved steadily and was discharged on 24/11/2020 in recovering condition. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks, including repeat chest imaging if clinically indicated. Isolation and hygiene measures were discussed with the patient prior to discharge. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician], Internal Medicine</div>"
            },
